+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+The registry owns validation of model-supplied tool input against the same JSON Schema definition that providers receive.
+
+## Contract
+
+- `execute` returns a descriptive `ToolResponse` for missing required fields, wrong types and enum violations before executing the tool; diagnostics and logs identify property paths and constraints without input values, while valid input, extra keys and context pass through unchanged exactly once without coercion or defaults, and unknown names still throw `Unknown tool: <name>`. ([validated by: rejects malformed tool input privately and passes valid input through unchanged](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L19)).
+- Static schemas compile during registration, are reused across ten executions, and uncompilable schemas throw during registration with the tool name in the error. ([validated by: compiles static schemas at registration and reuses them across ten calls](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L68)).
+- Function-valued definitions resolve on each execution and validate against the current schema, caching compilation by resolved schema object identity. ([validated by: validates dynamic definitions against the current schema and caches each schema object](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L95)).
